<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!-- SpotBugs project decisions: a rule, or a rule in part of the code, that the team has decided not
     to enforce. One Match per decision, with a comment giving the reason, for example:

       <!- - JPA entities share associations by design (reason ...) - ->
       <Match><Package name="~team\.projectpulse\..*"/><Bug pattern="EI_EXPOSE_REP"/></Match>

     Unlike the baseline, this file may grow, but every entry is a reviewed decision. -->
<FindBugsFilter>
    <!-- D1 (assignment 4): EI_EXPOSE_REP and EI_EXPOSE_REP2 are off for the whole project.
         All 219 findings are one of two designs Project Pulse relies on:
         1. JPA entities (Activity, PeerEvaluation, Section, ...) hand out and keep their collections and
            associations. Hibernate tracks changes through the collection the entity holds, and services
            edit entities through their getters (e.g. section.getTeams().add(...)), so a defensive copy
            would silently stop those changes from being saved.
         2. Spring beans (controllers, services, converters) keep the dependencies injected into their
            constructors; sharing that reference is how dependency injection works.
         Recheck if Project Pulse adds a class outside these two kinds that holds a mutable List, Map or Date. -->
    <Match>
        <Or>
            <Bug pattern="EI_EXPOSE_REP"/>
            <Bug pattern="EI_EXPOSE_REP2"/>
        </Or>
    </Match>
</FindBugsFilter>
